g that asks\nquestions the plan claims no learning outcome for - exactly the identity serve.py's own\ndropped-unit comment says must never break. No teacher SAW a misplaced question in SS (SS is\nitem-self-sufficient: its items carry period_ref and its port has always read it), and the LP\nnever displays LOs, so this was invisible on screen and would surface only in a coverage audit\n- but it was real, it was shipped, and it is now closed. The ANCHOR half remains latent on the\ncurrent corpus: science·secondary is the only handoff-bridged stage certified so far and its one\ncross-plan borrow carries no items.\n\nWHAT WAS BUILT (4 files, engine bumped e15 -> e16):\n1. aruvi_core/link_resolver.py - `platform_anchor(item)`: the platform's own stamp\n   (period_ref, then unit_ref) beats every subject join. Documented with the measured drift.\n2. The three joining ports now read it first and fall back to their own mediator only for an\n   UN-SERVED library file: science/subject.py:315, english/subject.py:299 (the positional\n   pairing counter still advances, so a stamped item cannot shift its siblings),\n   mathematics/subject.py:248 and :290. social_sciences and the_world_around_us were already\n   correct and are untouched - they are the reference behaviour this makes universal.\n3. science/subject.py grouping now keys on the item's OWN section_label, not on the mediating\n   number (the heading half of the defect).\n4. serve.py carries a borrowed SERVED unit's handoff row, remapped to the fill sitting, with an\n   `_order` beyond the host's rows so it reads last. Safe verbatim because the engine handoff is\n   label-keyed (carriers.to_engine_handoff chose that key for this exact reason).\n\nVERIFICATION.\n* NEW TEST tests/test_borrowed_anchor.py - the case the corpus withholds: a science·secondary-\n  shaped library whose borrowed unit CARRIES two questions and whose lender numbers them 6,\n  where the host's section 6 is a different section on a SERVED sitting. It i